        "kind": "argument",
        "name": "conditional_debt_forecast",
        "rationale": "Repeatedly using one maintained lifecycle and reviewed extension seams can reduce duplicated maintenance sites, conflicting behaviour and architectural drift during comparable later changes. This is a conditional mechanism, not an observed causal effect. It depends on later agents retrieving and applying current guidance, reviewers finding inappropriate abstractions, suitable tests, and repeated tasks; a single implementation does not measure future debt.",
